The reduced knee and loaded-cup demonstrations each implement six connections. On each side, Ia excites its own MN and inhibits the antagonist MN, and Ib inhibits its own MN. The Ia block combines a position signal and signed velocity and clips its output to \qtyrange{0}{10}{
ano\ampere}. For knee angle $q$ and angular range $R$, the extensor velocity input is $\dot q/R$. The implemented flexor path applies a second gain of $-1/R$ to that signal, giving $-\dot q/R^2$. In the cup model, the two muscles receive opposite signed deviations and velocities, each divided by \qty{0.3}{adian}. Both models feed tensile force directly to Ib. The knee's extensor and flexor gains are 0.0200 and \qty{0.0222}{
ano\ampere\per
ewton}, respectively. Both cup gains are \qty{0.008}{
ano\ampere\per
ewton}. The knee uses a simplified linear actuator. In the cup, filtered activation $A$ supplies $620A$\,kPa to each characterized BPA20 block. Neither circuit has an independent group II or foot-contact input.

I ran a control and a stimulated trial continuously for \qty{50}{\second} from the same initial knee flexion of \qty{0.26}{adian}, zero angular velocity and activation, and MN voltages of \qty{-52}{\milli\volt}. Tonic drive was \qty{4.2}{
ano\ampere} to the extensor MN and \qty{2.5}{
ano\ampere} to the flexor MN. In the stimulated trial I added \qty{2}{
ano\ampere} at \path{SN_Ia_ext}, after the spindle transducer and before the extensor Ia sensory-neuron membrane, for $30.000\leq t<30.030$\,s. Angle, speed, six membrane states, and two activations settled before stimulation. I report the negative of the model's internal flexion coordinate so that positive excursions indicate extension. The baseline was the mean control angle for $25\leq t<30$\,s, \ang{-42.6392}. The initial extension came from increased extensor force, which rose from \qty{7.37}{
ewton} at pulse onset to \qty{25.94}{
ewton} at pulse offset. The flexor MN output was zero at baseline, and flexor force was negligible during the pulse. Flexor force subsequently exceeded \qty{0.001}{
ewton} at \qty{38}{\milli\second} after onset and reached \qty{14.4}{
ewton} before maximum knee extension.

